BRAND: {"tone": "Warm, practical and restrained.", "voice_style": "Plain spoken English that translates supported features into ordinary situations.", "dos": ["Preserve exact trim and engine scope.", "Distinguish manufacturer descriptions from measured results.", "Keep unsupported questions as gaps."], "donts": ["Do not claim superiority or guarantees absent from evidence.", "Do not imply customer-specific context.", "Do not invent timing, mileage, capacity or safety results."], "persona_hint": "A product guide; inferred restrained profile, not an uploaded brand guideline."}
PLAN: {"customer_persona": "Compact-SUV shoppers comparing driving choices, passenger and luggage space, comfort features and ownership costs. Their personal priorities, daily route, location, budget and household remain unknown until they volunteer them.", "decision_frame": "The strongest fit is the engine and trim whose gearbox, seating and equipment match what you need, and the thing still to verify is that exact version\u2019s current on-road quote.", "takeaway": "Choose the engine and trim together, then confirm the features and current on-road cost of that exact version.", "primary_outcome": "Identify an engine-and-trim combination to check against the buyer\u2019s actual needs.", "supporting_outcomes": ["Understand the supported seating, comfort and assistance choices.", "Separate the current quote and missing evidence from the features already established."], "concerns": [{"topic": "powertrain", "why": "The separate engines have different gearbox pairings, while actual performance and fuel-use measurements are absent.", "fact_ids": ["F003", "F005", "F006", "F008", "F009"]}, {"topic": "space-and-practicality", "why": "The seat arrangement supports flexibility but the sources cannot establish personal passenger, luggage or parking fit.", "fact_ids": ["F001", "F021", "F022", "F023", "F024", "F063"]}, {"topic": "safety", "why": "Standard airbags and selected-trim assistance are different equipment choices and do not establish a crash rating.", "fact_ids": ["F025", "F031", "F033", "F034"]}, {"topic": "ownership", "why": "The conflicting dated entry price is not a current local on-road quote, and petrol extended warranty is separately paid.", "fact_ids": ["F054", "F055", "F056", "F057", "F058"]}, {"topic": "running-costs", "why": "Fuel-economy measurements, service costs and resale evidence are not supplied.", "fact_ids": []}], "usps": [{"id": "choose-your-gears", "name": "Choose how you change gears", "fact_ids": ["F003", "F005", "F006", "F008", "F009"], "stop_id": "powertrain"}, {"id": "share-the-room", "name": "Make space for people and bags", "fact_ids": ["F022", "F023"], "stop_id": "space-and-practicality"}, {"id": "airbags-from-the-start", "name": "Airbags included from the starting trim", "fact_ids": ["F025"], "stop_id": "safety"}], "segments": [{"id": "opening", "title": "The gearbox you use every day", "role": "intro", "goal": "MOMENT \u2014 Begin with the CRETA\u2019s supported manual-or-automatic choice for the petrol and diesel engines, without a second greeting or a claimed driving benefit. SPOKEN / DEEPER \u2014 One 30-word batch uses F003, F008 and F009 to explain choosing a manual gearbox or an automatic subject to engine and trim, with the complete transmission specifications held for deeper answers. VISUAL / HANDOFF \u2014 Open on the manual lever and console in im_pdf_df8fadffe78c7af4bbc1, the literal example of the manual choice rather than proof of an automatic selector, and leave the gearbox choice in focus with no checkin.", "outcome": "", "topic": "powertrain", "fact_ids": ["F003", "F008", "F009"], "usp_ids": ["choose-your-gears"], "visual_refs": ["im_pdf_df8fadffe78c7af4bbc1"], "priority_topic": false, "stop_id": null, "fundamental": false, "word_budget": 30}, {"id": "three-choices", "title": "Your gears, seating and airbags", "role": "outcome", "goal": "MOMENT \u2014 Give exactly three memorable anchors and say that the buyer can steer by interrupting, without asking another question. SPOKEN / DEEPER \u2014 One 33-word batch names the three reviewed USPs using F003/F005/F006/F008/F009, F022/F023 and F025, retaining that gearbox choice depends on engine and trim and the turbo is automatic-only. VISUAL / HANDOFF \u2014 Start on the manual lever im_pdf_df8fadffe78c7af4bbc1, change to the boot with sample bags im_pdf_06dc900e0519722a9b8a for storage context and the cabin panorama im_pdf_f422a4dec2ba86f0f22f for occupant context, never presenting the latter two as folded-seat or airbag proof, and leave the seating area in focus with an empty checkin.", "outcome": "Pick the buying choice that matters", "topic": "highlights", "fact_ids": ["F003", "F005", "F006", "F008", "F009", "F022", "F023", "F025"], "usp_ids": ["choose-your-gears", "share-the-room", "airbags-from-the-start"], "visual_refs": ["im_pdf_df8fadffe78c7af4bbc1", "im_pdf_06dc900e0519722a9b8a", "im_pdf_f422a4dec2ba86f0f22f"], "priority_topic": false, "stop_id": null, "fundamental": false, "word_budget": 33}, {"id": "engines", "title": "The engines and the brake-holding button", "role": "proof", "goal": "MOMENT \u2014 B1 opens on the gear lever as a choice about how to change gears, B2 opens on choosing the separate turbo engine, and B3 opens on the brake-holding button during a possible pause in traffic. SPOKEN / DEEPER \u2014 Assign B1 31 words to F003/F008/F009 for non-turbo petrol or diesel with manual/automatic choices depending on trim, B2 31 words to F003/F005/F006 for turbo petrol with an automatic only and listed solely on King without making every King a turbo, and B3 30 words to F015/F016 for stationary holding without keeping the brake pressed, standard from King; hold the S(O), S(O) Knight and SX Premium automatic-only auto-hold rows and unresolved S(O) Knight automatic combination in deeper beside F013/F014\u2019s exact automatic scope, F004/F007\u2019s complete power/torque units and engine-speed basis, and F002/F010/F011/F012 as manufacturer positioning/descriptions rather than measured driving results. VISUAL / HANDOFF \u2014 Use im_pdf_df8fadffe78c7af4bbc1 then im_pdf_d62b85cb6c76c3c1a60e for B1, im_pdf_eb83000c135195546031 for B2 and im_pdf_7f6a4cea202b824c4a74 for B3, mark the missing non-turbo petrol image and automatic controls explicitly rather than reusing a wrong engine, and hand off gearbox choice, driving controls and road contact in turn across 92 words with empty checkins.", "outcome": "Choose an engine and gearbox combination", "topic": "powertrain", "fact_ids": ["F002", "F003", "F004", "F005", "F006", "F007", "F008", "F009", "F010", "F011", "F012", "F013", "F014", "F015", "F016"], "usp_ids": ["choose-your-gears"], "visual_refs": ["im_pdf_eb83000c135195546031", "im_pdf_d62b85cb6c76c3c1a60e", "im_pdf_df8fadffe78c7af4bbc1", "im_pdf_90ccaf0bef2da9143187", "im_pdf_7f6a4cea202b824c4a74"], "priority_topic": true, "stop_id": "powertrain", "fundamental": true, "word_budget": 92}, {"id": "wheels", "title": "The wheels beneath the body", "role": "proof", "goal": "MOMENT \u2014 Notice the visible wheels in the whole-car view and separate the appearance choice from an unmeasured ride result. SPOKEN / DEEPER \u2014 One 27-word batch uses F017 for steel versus alloy choices that change by trim, with exact wheel-to-trim mapping and full F064 tyre sizes held deeper; no clearance, suspension or comfort result follows from those specifications. VISUAL / HANDOFF \u2014 Start on the whole side profile im_pdf_f9bbe411c2dac4280a3e where both wheels can be located, use im_pdf_654ca5b2d4cb084d4a92 only as additional whole-car context, and leave the body and cabin above the wheels as the next subject, with no checkin and no claim that the photographed wheel identifies every option.", "outcome": "Choose wheel style without assuming comfort", "topic": "stance-and-ride", "fact_ids": ["F017", "F064"], "usp_ids": [], "visual_refs": ["im_pdf_654ca5b2d4cb084d4a92", "im_pdf_f9bbe411c2dac4280a3e"], "priority_topic": false, "stop_id": "stance-and-ride", "fundamental": true, "word_budget": 27}, {"id": "space", "title": "The boot and the rear seatbacks", "role": "proof", "goal": "MOMENT \u2014 Open on the luggage in the boot as a possible occasion when passengers and bags must share the car. SPOKEN / DEEPER \u2014 One 33-word batch uses F022/F023 to explain the standard split rear seat\u2019s seating/storage flexibility and F021/F024 for rear passengers adjusting the seatback angle from S(O), with F001/F020/F059/F060/F063, the exact split ratio and absent capacity/legroom measurements reserved for deeper; reserve F061 for the disjoint storage batch later. VISUAL / HANDOFF \u2014 Begin on the literal sample luggage in im_pdf_06dc900e0519722a9b8a and change to the rear-seat area of im_pdf_f422a4dec2ba86f0f22f as contextual imagery only, because neither folding nor recline operation is shown, then leave the occupants\u2019 seats in focus with no checkin or promise that particular bags fit.", "outcome": "Arrange seating and luggage together", "topic": "space-and-practicality", "fact_ids": ["F001", "F020", "F021", "F022", "F023", "F024", "F059", "F060", "F061", "F063"], "usp_ids": ["share-the-room"], "visual_refs": ["im_pdf_f422a4dec2ba86f0f22f", "im_pdf_06dc900e0519722a9b8a", "im_pdf_8bfe17bdf06959cc1e40"], "priority_topic": true, "stop_id": "space-and-practicality", "fundamental": true, "word_budget": 33}, {"id": "safety", "title": "The seats and the help beside your lane", "role": "proof", "goal": "MOMENT \u2014 B1 opens around the visible seating area to explain standard occupant equipment, while B2 opens on the lane-detection diagram and the choice of additional driving assistance. SPOKEN / DEEPER \u2014 B1 uses 31 words with F025 for the six driver, passenger, side and curtain airbags fitted from E, explaining that this equipment does not require a higher trim; B2 uses 31 words with F031/F033/F034 for lane-keeping assistance on King, King Knight and Lounge Edition with the driver still attentive and responsible, while F026\u2013F030/F032/F035/F036/F062 stay deeper with standard equipment, camera availability from SX Premium and adaptive stop-go restricted to King/King Knight/Lounge automatics, without any inferred crash score or guaranteed intervention. VISUAL / HANDOFF \u2014 Use im_pdf_f422a4dec2ba86f0f22f as explicitly contextual seating imagery for B1 and im_pdf_2814e44d0603eba5c07b as the literal lane-detection illustration for B2, never inventing visible airbags or a demonstrated correction, and hand off occupants then the driver\u2019s controls across 62 words with no checkins.", "outcome": "Distinguish standard equipment and driving assistance", "topic": "safety", "fact_ids": ["F025", "F026", "F027", "F028", "F029", "F030", "F031", "F032", "F033", "F034", "F035", "F036", "F062"], "usp_ids": ["airbags-from-the-start"], "visual_refs": ["im_pdf_2814e44d0603eba5c07b", "im_pdf_f422a4dec2ba86f0f22f"], "priority_topic": true, "stop_id": "safety", "fundamental": true, "word_budget": 62}, {"id": "controls", "title": "Your temperature settings and phone connection", "role": "proof", "goal": "MOMENT \u2014 B1 begins at the dashboard with two front occupants who might prefer different temperature settings, and B2 begins with connecting a compatible phone. SPOKEN / DEEPER \u2014 Assign B1 31 words to F039/F040 for driver and front passenger choosing temperature settings independently from S(O), and B2 32 words to F045/F046 for wireless Android Auto/Apple CarPlay from EX with the wired-to-wireless adapter required from SX and device compatibility retained; hold F041/F042\u2019s complete screen dimensions, F043\u2019s three complimentary years and 70+ features subject to power/network, F044\u2019s Alexa Home to Car from SX with separate Alexa hardware excluded, and F047\u2019s front power seats/driver memory from King in deeper without inventing phone-app engine start. VISUAL / HANDOFF \u2014 Use the dashboard and front console in im_pdf_d0648e7a506c339014a1 for both batches as contextual imagery, describing only the visible dashboard rather than imaginary temperature readouts or an active phone link, and leave the occupants\u2019 settings then the cabin experience in focus across 63 words with empty checkins.", "outcome": "Choose individual settings and compatible connections", "topic": "cabin-and-tech", "fact_ids": ["F039", "F040", "F041", "F042", "F043", "F044", "F045", "F046", "F047"], "usp_ids": [], "visual_refs": ["im_pdf_d0648e7a506c339014a1"], "priority_topic": false, "stop_id": "cabin-and-tech", "fundamental": false, "word_budget": 63}, {"id": "comfort", "title": "Air through the seats and the roof above", "role": "proof", "goal": "MOMENT \u2014 B1 considers settling into a front seat on a warm evening and notices the airflow arrows, while B2 looks upward to the glass roof before mentioning the sound-system choice. SPOKEN / DEEPER \u2014 B1 uses 31 words with F037/F038 for cool airflow through the front-seat cushions from SX Premium, without a measured cooling-time or refrigerated-air claim; B2 uses 31 words with F048/F049 for the panoramic roof from EX(O), voice opening/closing from SX and F050 for the Bose sound option from SX Premium, keeping its full eight-speaker/subwoofer specification and F051/F052/F053\u2019s qualified lamp/glove-box details deeper rather than creating another delighters batch. VISUAL / HANDOFF \u2014 Start B1 on the literal seat-airflow illustration im_pdf_eef9a17053efd1f47451, B2 on the interior roof view im_pdf_2eaa12b3086c47d07a0f and use im_pdf_d0648e7a506c339014a1 solely as contextual cabin imagery if the sound system is named, leaving front-seat comfort then optional cabin equipment in focus within 62 words and no checkins.", "outcome": "Choose seat airflow roof and sound", "topic": "delighters", "fact_ids": ["F037", "F038", "F048", "F049", "F050", "F051", "F052", "F053"], "usp_ids": [], "visual_refs": ["im_pdf_eef9a17053efd1f47451", "im_pdf_2eaa12b3086c47d07a0f", "im_pdf_4f9cd789de81af3fa67e", "im_pdf_d0648e7a506c339014a1"], "priority_topic": false, "stop_id": "delighters", "fundamental": false, "word_budget": 62}, {"id": "price", "title": "The quote for your chosen version", "role": "proof", "goal": "MOMENT \u2014 Open with the limit that a starting price does not tell the buyer what a selected engine and trim will cost locally. SPOKEN / DEEPER \u2014 One 29-word batch uses F055/F056 for tax, registration and insurance added to the ex-showroom amount and a current dealer quotation, keeping F054\u2019s dated 19 September 2026 entry amount of \u20b910,90,700 and conflicting \u20b910.79 lakh structured value together in deeper; reserve F057/F058 for establish so the warranty claim is not repeated. VISUAL / HANDOFF \u2014 Use the whole-car side view im_pdf_f9bbe411c2dac4280a3e only as contextual imagery because no actual quotation or price graphic is supplied, leave the exact version and its quote in focus, and keep the checkin empty.", "outcome": "Obtain a current itemised on-road quote", "topic": "ownership", "fact_ids": ["F054", "F055", "F056", "F057", "F058"], "usp_ids": [], "visual_refs": ["im_pdf_f9bbe411c2dac4280a3e"], "priority_topic": true, "stop_id": "ownership", "fundamental": false, "word_budget": 29}, {"id": "armrest", "title": "Storage beside the front seat", "role": "features", "goal": "MOMENT \u2014 Notice the open armrest compartment beside the front seat as an additional place for everyday small items, without asserting that any particular item fits. SPOKEN / DEEPER \u2014 One 26-word batch uses F061 for standard front armrest storage and sliding adjustment only from King, retaining the exact continuous run King, King Knight and Lounge Edition and adding no cooling, locking or capacity claim. VISUAL / HANDOFF \u2014 Open and stay on the literal open compartment im_pdf_8bfe17bdf06959cc1e40, leave the front seat and chosen equipment in focus, and count this as the second and final space-and-practicality batch with no checkin.", "outcome": "Locate standard storage and optional adjustment", "topic": "space-and-practicality", "fact_ids": ["F061"], "usp_ids": [], "visual_refs": ["im_pdf_8bfe17bdf06959cc1e40"], "priority_topic": false, "stop_id": null, "fundamental": false, "word_budget": 26}, {"id": "terms-and-unknowns", "title": "The version and documents to confirm", "role": "establish", "goal": "MOMENT \u2014 End by keeping engine and trim together and naming the remaining source checks before a purchase decision. SPOKEN / DEEPER \u2014 One 33-word batch gives the variant-choice instruction, states F057/F058\u2019s separately paid petrol-only extended warranty, and directs the missing engine-specific fuel-economy evidence and exact-model/year crash report to Hyundai\u2019s official documents; hold the up-to-seven-years warranty limit, absent coverage/prices, stock, delivery and booking destination in deeper, with no repeat of the price claim. VISUAL / HANDOFF \u2014 Hold im_pdf_654ca5b2d4cb084d4a92 as contextual imagery of the car rather than a policy or a crash-test result, leave the unresolved documentation as the subject for the final summary and contact action, and count this as ownership\u2019s second batch with no checkin.", "outcome": "Know the terms and missing evidence", "topic": "ownership", "fact_ids": ["F057", "F058"], "usp_ids": [], "visual_refs": ["im_pdf_654ca5b2d4cb084d4a92"], "priority_topic": true, "stop_id": null, "fundamental": false, "word_budget": 33}], "ctas": [{"id": "dealer-contact", "label": "Request dealer contact", "kind": "contact", "url": "", "primary": true, "when": "end"}, {"id": "drive-contact", "label": "Request a test drive", "kind": "contact", "url": "", "primary": false, "when": "end"}], "voice": {"persona_name": "Priya", "persona_description": "The guide is a warm, practical product guide who follows the buyer\u2019s attention. The guide explains one useful thought at a time and says plainly which answers still need evidence.", "tone": "Cheerful and attentive Indian English, with short connected thoughts, restrained pauses and no pressure.", "sample_line": "Hi, welcome to the Hyundai CRETA; would you like to share what you\u2019re looking for in your next car, or shall we get started?", "suggested_voice": "priya", "language": "en-IN"}, "intake": {"q1": "Hi, welcome to the Hyundai CRETA; would you like to share what you\u2019re looking for in your next car, or shall we get started?", "q2": "", "chips": [{"key": "powertrain", "label": "Engines and gears"}, {"key": "stance-and-ride", "label": "Wheels and roads"}, {"key": "space-and-practicality", "label": "Seats and luggage"}, {"key": "safety", "label": "Safety and assistance"}, {"key": "cabin-and-tech", "label": "Controls and phone"}, {"key": "delighters", "label": "Seat airflow and roof"}, {"key": "ownership", "label": "Price and ownership"}]}, "do_not_recommend_if": "Do not recommend a particular version while a non-negotiable requirement depends on missing fuel-economy, safety-test, personal-fit, price or availability evidence.", "advance": "When the buyer is ready to verify a version, name Request dealer contact so the selected Hyundai dealer can confirm the engine and trim and provide a current itemised on-road quotation; the app records the contact preference and optional follow-up, not completed contact or a booking.", "notes": "Seven required Coach stops remain intact and ordered, and all three USP objects are copied exactly; no playbook version was supplied. Guided word allocation totals 427: powertrain 31+31+30, wheels 27, space 33, safety 31+31, cabin 31+32, delighters 31+31, price 29, supplemental armrest storage 26, and establish 33. These 14 main batches each stay within 26\u201333 words; adding the separate 23-word Explore overview and 45-word closing reaches the full 495-word target. Supplemental storage counts as space\u2019s second batch and establish as ownership\u2019s second, so every library stop remains at most two except powertrain\u2019s three. The Browse intro/outcome are separate at 30 and 33 words. Only the final fit summary and CTA receive closing statements, within the 45-word allowance; all segment checkins stay empty. Reordered batches stand alone and vary their opening through a visible detail, situation, choice or honest limit. Features and establish voice disjoint facts rather than repeating proof claims. The registry alone supports claims; supplied PDF images are visual context, with missing literal mechanisms explicitly flagged. No measured performance, comfort, safety or financial result is inferred. Technical quantities retain complete units and basis in deeper answers; the conflicting dated entry price remains a qualified deeper answer. Unknown customer context remains unknown, and the final summary names no preferred trim before the buyer supplies a reason. Retain configured Sarvam Priya; all CTAs are empty-URL contact requests because the source supplied no action destination.", "total_words": 495, "playbook_version": "2026-09-23", "guided_minimum_seconds": 180.0, "guided_opening_words": 23, "narration_preparation": {"version": 1, "target_words": 495, "identity": "f1675284b2049ed6dd8f7ad8493f2705639c611777f99c863c021f05e69d4a83"}}

FACT REGISTRY — the only allowed source of facts:
F001 [spec·stated] Body and driveline: five-door, five-seat compact SUV (conditions: All variants; manufacturer compilation dated 19 September 2026) (source: src_0cf1fd; locator: PDF page 3; quote: "The Hyundai CRETA is a five-door, five-seat compact SUV built by Hyundai Motor India and sold with front-wheel\ndrive across the whole range.")
F002 [claim·stated] Intended use: city use while still being capable on longer runs (conditions: Manufacturer positioning; not measured superiority) (source: src_0cf1fd; locator: PDF page 3; quote: "Hyundai positions the car as an SUV that works for city use while still being capable on longer runs.")
F003 [spec·stated] Engine choice: 1.5 l MPi petrol; 1.5 l U2 CRDi diesel; 1.5 l Turbo GDi petrol (source: src_0cf1fd; locator: PDF page 4; quote: "1.5 l MPi petrol; 1.5 l U2 CRDi diesel; 1.5 l Turbo GDi petrol")
F004 [spec·stated] Turbo maximum power: 117.5 kW (160 PS) @ 5,500 r/min (conditions: 1.5 l Turbo GDi petrol; specification, not an acceleration measurement) (source: src_0cf1fd; locator: PDF page 16; quote: "117.5 kW (160 PS) @\n5,500 r/min")
F005 [spec·stated] Turbo transmission: 7-speed DCT (conditions: Turbo petrol only; DCT means dual-clutch automatic) (source: src_0cf1fd; locator: PDF page 16; quote: "1.5 l Turbo GDi petrol\n1,482 cm³\n117.5 kW (160 PS) @\n5,500 r/min\n253 Nm (25.8 kgm) @\n1,500–3,500 r/min\n7-speed DCT")
F006 [availability·stated] Turbo trim availability: King (conditions: Column headers E, EX, EX(O), S(O), S(O) Knight, SX, SX Premium, King, King Knight, Lounge Edition. Only King is marked for turbo/DCT. King also offers other engines; do not imply every King is turbo.) (source: src_0cf1fd; locator: PDF page 31; quote: "1.5 l turbo GDi petrol\nDCT\n –\n –\n –\n –\n –\n –\n –\n ●\n –\n –")
F007 [spec·stated] Diesel torque: 250 Nm (25.5 kgm) @ 1,500–2,750 r/min (conditions: 1.5 l U2 CRDi diesel; not a loaded-climb performance test) (source: src_0cf1fd; locator: PDF page 16; quote: "250 Nm (25.5 kgm) @\n1,500–2,750 r/min")
F008 [spec·stated] Diesel transmission choices: 6-speed manual or 6-speed automatic (conditions: Trim combinations differ; see engine matrix page 31) (source: src_0cf1fd; locator: PDF page 16; quote: "1.5 l U2 CRDi diesel\n1,493 cm³\n85 kW (116 PS) @ 4,000\nr/min\n250 Nm (25.5 kgm) @\n1,500–2,750 r/min\n6-speed manual or\n6-speed automatic")
F009 [spec·stated] Petrol transmission choices: 6-speed manual or IVT (conditions: Naturally aspirated petrol; trim combinations differ) (source: src_0cf1fd; locator: PDF page 16; quote: "1.5 l MPi petrol\n1,497 cm³\n84.4 kW (115 PS) @ 6,300\nr/min\n143.8 Nm (14.7 kgm) @ 4,500\nr/min\n6-speed manual or IVT")
F010 [claim·stated] Turbo manufacturer driving description: impressive power, smooth acceleration, and responsive handling (conditions: Hyundai marketing description, not a measured test result; never imply an acceleration time or guaranteed overtaking) (source: src_0cf1fd; locator: PDF page 16; quote: "It delivers\nimpressive power, smooth acceleration, and responsive handling for a thrilling yet refined drive across city roads and\nhighways alike")
F011 [claim·stated] Diesel manufacturer driving description: strong torque, high fuel efficiency, and quiet performance (conditions: Hyundai marketing, not mileage or noise measurements) (source: src_0cf1fd; locator: PDF page 16; quote: "The robust 1.5L U2 CRDi diesel engine, available with 6-speed manual and automatic transmissions, delivers strong\ntorque, high fuel efficiency, and quiet performance.")
F012 [claim·stated] Petrol manufacturer use description: everyday practicality with refined driving comfort (conditions: Hyundai marketing. Do not convert superior fuel economy to a comparative test or mileage figure.) (source: src_0cf1fd; locator: PDF page 16; quote: "It combines everyday practicality with refined driving comfort, ensuring consistent\npower delivery and superior fuel economy.")
F013 [feature·stated] Drive and traction modes by trim: Normal, Eco, Sport; Snow, Mud and Sand (conditions: Automatic cars only in the listed trims; no automatic SX listed in engine matrix; S(O) Knight matrix has no current automatic combination) (source: src_0cf1fd; locator: PDF page 17; quote: "Drive mode select and the Snow, Mud and Sand traction control modes are fitted to automatic cars only, and appear on S(O), S(O) Knight, SX\nPremium, King, King Knight and Lounge Edition.")
F014 [feature·stated] Paddle shifters function: quick gear changes (conditions: Automatic cars on S(O), S(O) Knight, SX Premium, King, King Knight, Lounge Edition per p39 starred row. Manufacturer function description; do not imply measured shift time.) (source: src_0cf1fd; locator: PDF page 17; quote: "Mounted behind the steering wheel, the paddle shifters enable quick gear changes for enhanced control and sporty\nperformance, making every drive more responsive and enjoyable.")
F015 [feature·stated] Auto hold function: holding the vehicle in place when stationary (conditions: Electronic parking brake with auto hold. S(O), S(O) Knight and SX Premium automatics; King, King Knight and Lounge standard per p39. No guarantee on all surfaces.) (source: src_0cf1fd; locator: PDF page 44; quote: "automatically holding the vehicle in place when stationary, eliminating the need to\nkeep the brake pressed.")
F016 [availability·stated] Auto hold applicability: Electric parking brake with auto hold (conditions: E, EX, EX(O): unavailable. S(O), S(O) Knight, SX Premium: automatic only. SX: unavailable. King, King Knight, Lounge: standard. Footnote * = IVT, AT or DCT only, p41.) (source: src_0cf1fd; locator: PDF page 39; quote: "Electric parking brake with auto hold\n –\n –\n –\n S*\n S*\n –\n S*\n S\n S\n S")
F017 [spec·stated] Wheel sizes by trim: R16, R17 and R18 (conditions: No comparative ride comfort or road-absorption claim follows from wheel size.) (source: src_0cf1fd; locator: PDF page 8; quote: "R16 steel with wheel cover\nE, EX\nR16 dual-tone styled steel\nEX(O)\nR17 black alloys\nS(O)\nR17 diamond cut alloys\nSX, SX Premium\nR18 diamond cut alloys\nKing\nR18 matte black alloys\nS(O) Knight, King Knight, Lounge Edition")
